course: dictionary
lesson: 12258
title: Contaminate: when something clean is spoiled
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: To contaminate something is to make it dirty, impure or harmful by adding something bad to it, such as germs, poison or chemicals. «Raw chicken juice can contaminate the salad if you use the same chopping board.» The salad is clean, so the chicken juice must be something that makes food unsafe.
explain: Look for clues in the words around the word. «Dirty test tubes can contaminate the results of our experiment.» Dirty test tubes are unwanted things, and results are spoiled by them. In science, contaminate means that something unwanted got into a sample and spoiled it.
explain: Contaminate can also mean a bad influence on someone. «His grumpy mood began to contaminate the whole team.» Nobody spilled anything here, but the mood spread and spoiled how everyone felt and worked. Ask yourself: what is being spoiled, and by what?
fact: Contaminate means to make something dirty, impure or harmful by adding something bad.
fact: In science, to contaminate a sample means to let something unwanted get into it and spoil the test.
fact: Oil spills and sewage can contaminate rivers and seas.
fact: Wash your hands and use separate chopping boards so germs do not contaminate your food.
fact: Contaminate is a verb: contaminates, contaminated and contaminating are its other forms.
exercise: «Raw chicken juice can contaminate the salad if you use the same chopping board.» What does contaminate mean here? | Store something in a cold place | *Make something unsafe by adding germs | Cut something into small pieces | Make something clean and fresh
exercise: «Dirty test tubes can contaminate the results of our experiment.» What is being spoiled? | The science teacher | *The results of the experiment | The test tubes | The lab coats
exercise: Copy the word from this sentence that means spoiled by something bad: «Oil from the spill began to contaminate the river.» | river | oil | *contaminate | spill
test: «Keep the poison away from the well, or it will contaminate the water.» What does contaminate mean? | *To make the water harmful by adding poison | To make the water colder | To make the water taste sweet | To pour the water into a jug
test: «His grumpy mood began to contaminate the whole team.» What does contaminate suggest? | The team was painting a wall | The team was given a prize | *His bad mood was spoiling how the team felt | The team went to sleep early
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to contaminate? | Protect | Polish | *Pollute | Purify
